{"reference":"1 Chronicles 7","book":"1 Chronicles","chapter":7,"status":"pending","sections":[{"kind":"surrounding_passages","title":"Reading the Genealogies","blocks":[{"id":"block_1","text":"The genealogies surrounding this chapter are best read as selective literary maps of kinship, land, office, and restored identity, rather than as exhaustive modern-style family trees. Gaps, parallel lines, differing names, and compressed generations may therefore need to be considered case by case.","verse_refs":["1 Chronicles 1:1-54","1 Chronicles 2:1-55","1 Chronicles 3:1-24","1 Chronicles 4:1-43","1 Chronicles 5:1-26","1 Chronicles 6:1-81","1 Chronicles 8:1-40","1 Chronicles 9:1-44"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_1_chronicles_007_d1f816fb78a4a77862ed2ecf"],"confidence":"high","interpretation_level":"disputed"}]}],"generated_metadata":null}